  "_torch_flash_note": "The torch_flash entry is load_bearing but deliberately carries NO median_ms. load_bearing is what makes check_regressions discover this shape as the speedup anchor; the ratio it then checks uses live measurements from both arms, not this baseline. Measured run-to-run spread on torch_flash's own absolute timing exceeds perf_drift_pct, so a timing baseline here would fire on noise while telling us nothing the ratio does not. Sage's own rows are stable well inside the threshold.",
  "_stability_note": "Rows are reproducible to well under perf_drift_pct on a settled GPU. A run started immediately after sustained prior load can show a large one-off transient on an individual row (observed once during promotion, on a non-load-bearing row, and not reproducible in three settled repeats). If a single row fires alone and implausibly, re-run on an idle GPU before investigating the kernel."
